# Ship-gate workflow

Start and finish product work from a Cursor agent request. Do not auto-commit, auto-push, auto-merge, auto-deploy, manually create a GitHub Release (deploy workflow creates it), or edit sibling website changelogs without an explicit user choice at each gate (or a prior explicit order that covers that gate).

## Gates

At each gate, end the turn with a numbered list of next best actions and **one recommended reply**. Wait for the user before continuing.

### Before PR — local dev verify

Present after focused tests pass and release metadata validates (`changelog-validate` vs `origin/main`), but **before** the commit gate.

**Recommended:** Run local dev verify on the PR branch (`composer pre-pr-verify` or the manual steps in `.cursor/skills/ship-gate/SKILL.md`), then continue to commit/PR.

1. Local verify passed — continue to commit/PR
2. Re-run local verify (install test with `-Fresh`)
3. Fix issues and retry
4. Skip local verify (document why)
5. Stop / leave as-is

Reuse an already-running preview; do not start duplicate servers. On Laragon use `http://myapes-account.test/` and `composer run dev:laragon`; otherwise `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` and `composer run dev`.

### Before PR / commit

**When to commit** (all that apply):

1. Slice on the `cursor/...` branch is complete (or the user wants a clear WIP checkpoint).
2. Focused tests for the change have been run (or failure is documented and the user still wants a commit).
3. If merging to `main`: release metadata is on the branch (`changelog-prepare`, TODOs filled, `changelog-validate` vs `origin/main`) — same PR as the work.
4. Local dev verify passed (or skip documented at the local verify gate).
5. Diff is free of secrets / unrelated files; message will explain *why*.

Prefer **not** to commit mid-edit with broken tests (unless WIP), before required release metadata, before local verify (unless skipped), or while scope is undecided. Mid-work commits only after an explicit pick below (or a prior “commit WIP” order) — no automatic checkpoint cadence.

Present this gate when work is ready for review, or when the user asks to save progress. **Recommended:** Commit and open/update PR when review-ready (release metadata included if needed). Prefer Commit only when a PR already exists and only the commit is missing.

1. Commit and open/update PR
2. Commit only (no push / no PR yet)
3. Commit WIP checkpoint (incomplete; message notes WIP)
4. Keep working uncommitted
5. Stop / leave as-is

Never commit or push unless the user already ordered it or picks 1–3.

### After PR CI is green

Recommended usually: merge when release metadata and checks are OK.

1. Merge the PR
2. Fix remaining review / CI issues
3. Leave PR open / stop

Never merge unless the user already ordered merge or picks option 1.

### After merge is verified on `main` — changelog hubs

App Change Log Hub (`/change-log`) is fed by `resources/data/releases.json` in **this** repo. Confirm the head record on `main` matches `VERSION`. **Live** hub verification waits until after Cloudron deploy; do not open a separate metadata PR for the hub.

Recommended: confirm metadata on `main`, then continue to the Cloudron deploy gate.

1. Changelog metadata on `main` looks good — continue to Cloudron deploy gate
2. Also update sibling website changelogs / hubs (name which sites after the user confirms)
3. Skip hub checks

Never edit `APESCIC/*` website repos or create issues there unless the user explicitly asks in this session.

### After changelog gate — Cloudron deploy

Recommended: deploy when main tests are green and pre-merge local verify already passed on the PR branch.

1. Deploy to Cloudron now
2. Skip deploy

Never assume Cloudron already updated. Deploy only via `workflow_dispatch` (see `.cursor/skills/ship-gate/SKILL.md`). Pass `app_version` from `VERSION` when dispatching.

### After Cloudron deploy succeeds — live hub and GitHub Release verification

Successful Cloudron deploy publishes the live Change Log Hub and runs **Publish GitHub Release** automatically (`{VERSION} Beta` display title; tag `v{VERSION}` on the deployed SHA).

Recommended: verify live `/change-log`, `healthz`, and the GitHub Release match the deployed version and SHA.

1. Verify live hub and GitHub Release for deployed version
2. Skip live verification

Never create a duplicate GitHub Release manually unless recovering from a failed publish job.

## Unchanged

Release **metadata** (`VERSION`, `releases.json`, contract) still ships in the **same PR** before merge (see release-metadata rule). That metadata is the source of truth for the MyAPES Core Change Log Hub after deploy.
